{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Do you not know that I divine, etc.</b> By this he intended to refute as well their claim — which they might make: Who revealed this secret to you that we are the thieves — unless one were to say that it was the doing of their own hands and he accomplished the thing. Therefore he said: ״הֲלֹא יְדַעְתֶּם כִּי נַחֵשׁ״ and so forth, and from this he knew." "And his saying <b>a man such as I.</b> Meaning: plainly, any great man such as I would divine to know hidden things that he can attain, and if so the matter would be revealed to me, and you should have been concerned about the matter — that it would not be beyond me."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:29.610075389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}